# Without this, a checkout on a machine with `core.autocrlf=true` (the
# common default on Windows, including GitHub's own `windows-latest`
# runner) silently rewrites any LF byte it thinks looks like a text file's
# line ending into CRLF — corrupting these binary formats byte-for-byte.
# Found via a real CI failure: the KDBX test fixtures decrypted to garbled,
# partial data on Windows only (`tests/fixtures/*.kdbx`), never on macOS or
# on this development machine, because nothing here ever exercised a fresh
# Windows checkout until CI actually ran one.
*.kdbx binary
*.key binary
*.icns binary
*.ico binary
*.rgba binary
